<article class="env-remark" id="05GS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05GS">Remark <span data-tag="05GS">15.26.5</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. When does $R$ satisfy the condition mentioned in Lemmas <a href="/tag/053A" data-tag="053A">15.26.1</a>, <a href="/tag/053B" data-tag="053B">15.26.2</a>, and <a href="/tag/053D" data-tag="053D">15.26.4</a>? This holds if </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$R$ is local, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$R$ is Noetherian, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$R$ is a domain, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$R$ is a reduced ring with finitely many minimal primes, or 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$R$ has finitely many weakly associated primes, see Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/05CB" data-tag="05CB">10.66.17</a>. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Thus these lemmas hold in all cases listed above. </p>
</article>